+# Summary
+
+**Status: `python -m unittest` is NOT fully green: 5 of 6 pass, 1 fails because the test contradicts `docs/PRICING.md`.**
+
+## Changed (`billing/invoice.py`)
+- `Line.vat` now uses `net * rate` (was `unit_price * rate`, which ignored quantity) — rule 3.
+- `Invoice.add` raises `ValueError` for rate names not in `RATES` — rule 3.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` before: 4 failures. After: 1 failure (`test_reduced_rate_small_item`).
+
+## Needs a decision
+`tests/test_invoice.py::test_reduced_rate_small_item` expects VAT 0.02 / gross 0.52 for a 0.50 item at the reduced rate. 0.50 × 0.05 = 0.025, and PRICING.md rule 4 explicitly says 0.025 becomes 0.03 (round half up). The code gives 0.03 (gross 0.53), which matches the docs. I did not edit the test or the docs. Either the test is stale (should expect 0.03 / 0.53), or finance's rule differs from what was signed off. Please confirm with finance; the release stays blocked on this test until then.
+
+## Not verified
+Nothing beyond the unit tests; no other callers exist in the repo.
